  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    user_intent: "Adding Binary Number Activities\nThe user wants to add a new section to the application focused on binary numbers. This involves creating a new button on the landing page that leads to a binary menu. From this menu, users can access four distinct interactive activities: \"Kabinet u\304\215itel\305\257\" (Teachers\' Office), \"\304\214\303\255slov\303\241n\303\255 \305\276\303\241k\305\257\" (Student Counting), \"Pravdivostn\303\255 tabulka\" (Truth Table), and \"S\304\215\303\255t\303\241n\303\255 bin\303\241rn\303\255ch \304\215\303\255sel\" (Binary Addition). Each of these activities needs to be implemented as a separate screen with its own interactive logic."
    session_summary: "The user wants to add a new section to the application focused on binary numbers. This involves creating several new interactive activities and integrating them into the app\'s navigation.\n\nHere\'s a summary of the work done:\n\n**1. New Feature: Binary Numbers Section**\n\n*   **Goal:** Introduce a new section dedicated to binary number concepts, including interactive activities.\n*   **New Activities:**\n    *   **Binary Menu (`BinaryMenu.tsx`):** A central menu for the binary section, providing access to individual activities.\n    *   **Teachers\' Office (`TeachersOffice.tsx`):** An activity simulating a teacher\'s office status using binary representation (present/absent) and visualizing the corresponding binary code and signal lights.\n    *   **Student Counting (`StudentCounting.tsx`):** An activity where users arrange students (representing bits) to form binary numbers and match a target decimal number.\n    *   **Truth Table (`TruthTable.tsx`):** An interactive truth table illustrating logical operations (AND, OR) in the context of academic conditions (no \'3\' grades, average <= 1.5).\n    *   **Binary Addition (`BinaryAddition.tsx`):** An activity where users practice adding binary numbers, including handling carries.\n*   **Navigation Integration:**\n    *   Added a new \"Bin\303\241rn\303\255 \304\215\303\255sla\" button to the `LandingPage.tsx`.\n    *   Updated `App.tsx` to handle the new screens (`binary-menu`, `teachers-office`, `student-counting`, `truth-table`, `binary-addition`) and their navigation logic.\n    *   Modified `types.ts` to include the new screen types.\n*   **Dependencies & APIs:**\n    *   Utilized `lucide-react` for icons (e.g., `Binary`, `Users`, `ListOrdered`, `Table`, `PlusCircle`, `ArrowLeft`, `HelpCircle`, `CheckCircle2`, `XCircle`, `Lightbulb`, `User`, `UserCheck`, `ChevronRight`, `ChevronLeft`, `RefreshCcw`).\n    *   Standard React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`) were used for state management and component logic.\n\n**2. Existing Feature Enhancements:**\n\n*   **Compression Game (`CompressionGame.tsx`):**\n    *   Added a new \"Vlastn\303\255\" (Custom) button to the level selection, allowing users to access a custom image compression activity.\n    *   Modified `CompressionGame.tsx` to include `onStartCustom` prop and handle the transition to the new `custom-compression` screen.\n*   **App Navigation (`App.tsx`):**\n    *   Updated `App.tsx` to route to the new `custom-compression` screen.\n\n**3. Project Setup & Tooling:**\n\n*   **`package.json`:** Added a `lint` script (`tsc --noEmit`) to improve code quality checks.\n\n**4. Design Decisions:**\n\n*   **Visual Theme:** Maintained the existing application\'s aesthetic with a focus on clean design, rounded corners, subtle gradients, and clear iconography. The new binary section uses an amber/orange color palette to distinguish it.\n*   **Interactivity:** Focused on making each activity interactive and providing immediate feedback to the user.\n*   **Educational Context:** The activities are designed to teach fundamental computer science concepts (binary representation, logic gates, data encoding) in an engaging way, drawing from the provided educational material.\n\n**5. Blockers & Bugs:**\n\n*   None identified during this session.\n\n**6. Next Steps:**\n\n*   **Implement remaining binary activities:** Create the actual components for `BinaryMenu`, `TeachersOffice`, `StudentCounting`, `TruthTable`, and `BinaryAddition`.\n*   **Refine existing components:** Ensure seamless integration and consistent UI/UX across all sections.\n*   **Testing:** Thoroughly test all new features and existing functionalities.\n*   **Content Review:** Double-check the educational accuracy and clarity of the content within the new activities."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>25-25</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added new screen types for binary-related activities to the Screen type definition.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/CompressionGame.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>118-120;220-234</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added `onStartCustom` prop to `CompressionGameProps` and a button to trigger the custom compression screen.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>13-15;46-51;61-67;127-129</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Imported new binary-related components and added new screen cases to the `renderScreen` function for navigation.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/LandingPage.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>6-11;38-80</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added `onStartBinary` prop to `LandingPageProps` and a new button for \"Bin\303\241rn\303\255 \304\215\303\255sla\" that navigates to the binary menu.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/BinaryMenu.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-91</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new `BinaryMenu` component with buttons for different binary-related activities (Teachers Office, Student Counting, Truth Table, Binary Addition) and navigation.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/TeachersOffice.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-121</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new `TeachersOffice` component to simulate the logic of two teachers\' presence using binary representation and visual feedback.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/StudentCounting.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-121</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new `StudentCounting` component that allows users to arrange students (representing bits) to form binary numbers and match a target decimal number.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/TruthTable.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-178</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new `TruthTable` component that allows users to fill in truth tables for AND and OR logic gates, with interactive elements and feedback.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/BinaryAddition.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>1-170</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new `BinaryAddition` component that allows users to perform binary addition by inputting the sum and carries, with validation and feedback.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/types.ts</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-26</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file defines the types used throughout the application, including `Screen` which was updated to include new binary-related screens.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/components/LandingPage.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-97</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file was modified to add a new button for \"Bin\303\241rn\303\255 \304\215\303\255sla\" that navigates to the new binary menu.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-140</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file was updated to import the new binary-related components and to add the navigation logic for these new screens within the `renderScreen` function.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>"
