    thinking: "**Constructing Path Finding Task**\n\nI\'m now creating `PathFindingTask.tsx` to build the pathfinding task. I\'m opting for a straightforward graph representation, enabling user input of paths as letter strings such as \"ABFH\" for clarity. I\'ve defined the graph with nodes A through H, and edges A-B, and A-C.\n\n\n**Refining Graph Connections**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously comparing the visual graph representation with the textual descriptions of valid paths. It seems there\'s a discrepancy that requires clarification. I\'m focusing on the edges described in both the graph and the paths. It\'s becoming critical to resolve the inconsistencies before I continue. I\'m starting to build a better understanding, though, especially with the textual descriptions.\n\n\n**Verifying Node Connections**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing the node connections from page 39\'s image with the textual path descriptions to resolve discrepancies. It turns out the edges are: A-B, A-C, B-D, B-E, B-F, C-D, D-F, E-G, F-G, F-H, and G-H. Using these edges, I\'m checking the paths again: ABFH, ABFGH, ABDFH, ABDFGH, and the edge sequence ACDBFH now works with the image.\n\n\n**Validating Path Representations**\n\nI\'ve just finished a meticulous edge verification, cross-checking all paths to confirm the accuracy of the implied connections. Thirteen valid paths now inform my graph\'s structure. I\'m satisfied with the resulting edge set; my next step is defining task levels based on these confirmed paths. I\'ve begun to sketch out 5 levels with progressively complex paths.\n\n\n**Defining Task Levels**\n\nI\'m now defining the edges and paths for levels 1 through 5, ensuring each level progressively increases in complexity. I\'ve also decided to use SVG to render the graphs and will use fixed coordinates for each node at each level. Level 5\'s node coordinates have been further refined to match the PDF graph\'s layout more closely.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
