    session_summary: "The user and I have been working on developing a React application. Here\'s a summary of our progress:\n\n**Features Modified, Added, or Removed:**\n\n*   **App.tsx:**\n    *   Imported `ModelsMenu`, `TimetableGraph`, and `PathFindingTask`.\n    *   Added a new screen case `\'path-finding\'` to the `renderScreen` switch statement to navigate to the `PathFindingTask` component.\n    *   Updated `ModelsMenu` component to include an `onStartPathFinding` prop.\n    *   Imported `BlatovTask`.\n    *   Added `\'blatov-task\'` to the `Screen` type in `types.ts`.\n    *   Added `onStartBlatov` prop to `ModelsMenuProps` and updated `ModelsMenu` to include a \"Bl\303\241tov\" button that navigates to `\'blatov-task\'`.\n    *   Added a new screen case `\'blatov-task\'` to the `renderScreen` switch statement to navigate to the `BlatovTask` component.\n*   **types.ts:**\n    *   Added `\'blatov-task\'` to the `Screen` type definition.\n*   **ModelsMenu.tsx:**\n    *   Added `onStartBlatov` to `ModelsMenuProps`.\n    *   Updated the `ModelsMenu` component to include a button for \"Bl\303\241tov\" that calls `onStartBlatov`.\n    *   Adjusted the grid layout to `lg:grid-cols-3` for better spacing on larger screens.\n    *   Modified container widths and margins for better responsiveness.\n*   **BlatovTask.tsx (New File):**\n    *   Created a new component `BlatovTask` to implement the \"Bl\303\241tov\" interactive task.\n    *   This task focuses on the concept of a \"Spanning Tree\" in graph theory.\n    *   It includes 5 levels of difficulty, each with a different graph structure.\n    *   The component features interactive SVG for graph visualization, allowing users to click on edges to form connections.\n    *   It includes logic for checking the validity of the solution (connectivity and minimum edges) and provides user feedback.\n    *   Navigation between levels and a reset functionality are implemented.\n    *   Includes a \"Did you know?\" section explaining the concept of Spanning Trees.\n*   **VectorDrawing.tsx:**\n    *   Modified to support two modes: `\'points\'` (drawing individual points) and `\'lines\'` (drawing connected line segments).\n    *   Implemented input fields for manually setting coordinates of new points.\n    *   Added functionality to remove individual points.\n    *   Enhanced the UI with better styling, scrollbars for the point list, and theme-based colors for different modes.\n    *   Added a preview line when drawing in `\'lines\'` mode.\n    *   Included a check to prevent adding the exact same point consecutively.\n*   **ColorMixer.tsx:**\n    *   Modified to handle both \'RGB\' and \'CMYK\' color mixing modes.\n    *   Implemented sliders for adjusting R, G, B values and C, M, Y, K values.\n    *   Added a visual representation of the mixed color.\n    *   Included explanations for RGB (additive) and CMYK (subtractive) color mixing.\n\n**Dependencies and APIs:**\n\n*   `react`: Core React library.\n*   `lucide-react`: Used for icons (e.g., `ArrowLeft`, `Plus`, `Map`, `Home`, `HelpCircle`, `CheckCircle2`, `XCircle`, `RefreshCcw`, `ChevronRight`, `ChevronLeft`, `Construction`, `MousePointer2`, `MapPin`, `List`, `Trash2`, `PenTool`).\n*   `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`: React hooks for state management and DOM manipulation.\n*   SVG: Used for graph and drawing visualizations.\n\n**Design Decisions:**\n\n*   **Component-based architecture**: The application is structured into reusable React components.\n*   **State management**: `useState` hook is used for managing component-level state.\n*   **Conditional rendering**: Used extensively to switch between different screens and modes.\n*   **Tailwind CSS**: Used for styling and layout.\n*   **SVG for graphics**: Chosen for its scalability and interactivity in visualizing graphs and drawings.\n*   **Clear navigation**: Implemented through a `screen` state in `App.tsx` and `onBack` props passed down to components.\n*   **Interactive feedback**: Visual cues (animations, color changes) are provided to the user for actions and state changes.\n\n**Existing Blockers and Bugs:**\n\n*   The error `Uncaught TypeError: Constructor Map requires \'new\'` was identified, likely stemming from incorrect usage of the `Map` constructor (e.g., calling it as a function instead of with `new`). The `grep` command indicated potential issues in `VectorDrawing.tsx`, `PathFindingTask.tsx`, and `ModelsMenu.tsx`. The fix for `Map` in `VectorDrawing.tsx` was not explicitly shown in the provided logs, but the general error suggests a need to review its usage.\n\n**Next Steps to Solve the Problem:**\n\n1.  **Address the `Map` constructor error**:\n    *   Review all instances where `Map` is used in the codebase, particularly in `VectorDrawing.tsx` and `PathFindingTask.tsx`.\n    *   Ensure that `new Map()` is used correctly and not just `Map()`.\n2.  **Compile and test the application**: After fixing the `Map` error, compile the applet again and thoroughly test all implemented features, especially the newly added \"Bl\303\241tov\" task and the updated \"Vector Drawing\" and \"Color Mixer\" components.\n3.  **Refine \"Vector Drawing\" mode switching**: Ensure the logic for switching between \'points\' and \'lines\' modes in `VectorDrawing.tsx` is robust and handles all edge cases correctly.\n4.  **Further testing of \"Bl\303\241tov\" task**: Verify the correctness of the spanning tree logic across all levels and ensure the user feedback is clear and helpful.\n5.  **Code cleanup and optimization**: Review the codebase for any potential areas of improvement in terms of performance, readability, and maintainability.\n\nThis summary should provide a clear picture of the current state of the project and the necessary steps to continue development."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>22-22</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added \'blatov-task\' to the Screen type union.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>5-5;12-12;18-18;20-20;23-23;26-26;33-33;36-36;42-42;45-45;52-52;55-55;62-62;65-65;71-71;74-74;83-83;86-86;89-89;90-90;91-91;92-92;93-93;94-94;95-95;96-96;97-97;98-98;99-99;100-100;101-101;102-102;103-103;104-104;105-105;106-106;107-107;108-108;109-109;110-110;111-111;112-112;113-113;114-114;115-115;116-116;117-117;118-118;119-119;120-120;121-121;122-122;123-123;124-124;125-125;126-126;127-127;128-128;129-129;130-130;131-131;132-132;133-133;134-134;135-135;136-136;137-137;138-138;139-139;140-140;141-141;142-142;143-143;144-144;145-145;146-146;147-147;148-148;149-149;150-150;151-151;152-152;153-153;154-154;155-155;156-156;157-157;158-158;159-159;160-160;161-161;162-162;163-163;164-164;165-165;166-166;167-167;168-168;169-169;170-170;171-171;172-172;173-173;174-174;175-175;176-176;177-177;178-178;179-179;180-180;181-181;182-182;183-183;184-184;185-185;186-186;187-187;188-188</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added `onStartBlatov` prop to `ModelsMenuProps` and the corresponding button in the JSX. Also updated the grid to `lg:grid-cols-3` and adjusted max-widths and margins for better layout.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>22-22;85-89;91-91</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Imported `BlatovTask` and added a new case for \'blatov-task\' in the `renderScreen` switch statement. Updated `ModelsMenu` to include the `onStartBlatov` prop.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/components/BlatovTask.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>0-364</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Created a new component `BlatovTask` for the Bl\303\241tov task. This component includes the game logic, UI for graph visualization, controls, and feedback for the spanning tree problem.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>0-188</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file is the main entry point of the application and handles routing between different screens. It was necessary to add imports and cases for the new Bl\303\241tov task.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>0-188</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file displays the menu for different models. It was modified to include a new button for the Bl\303\241tov task and to pass the necessary prop to handle the navigation.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/types.ts</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-25</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file defines the types used throughout the application, including the `Screen` type. It was updated to include the new \'blatov-task\' screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx: renderScreen switch statement</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The `renderScreen` function uses a switch statement to conditionally render different components based on the `currentScreen` state. A new case for \'blatov-task\' was added here to render the `BlatovTask` component.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>ModelsMenu.tsx: ModelsMenuProps interface</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The `ModelsMenuProps` interface defines the props that the `ModelsMenu` component accepts. The `onStartBlatov` function prop was added to this interface to enable navigation to the Bl\303\241tov task.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>ModelsMenu.tsx: ModelsMenu component JSX</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The JSX for the `ModelsMenu` component was updated to include a new button element. This button is configured to call the `onStartBlatov` prop when clicked, triggering the navigation to the Bl\303\241tov task.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>BlatovTask.tsx: BlatovTask component</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This is the newly created component for the Bl\303\241tov task. It contains the core logic for the spanning tree problem, including graph representation, user interaction for selecting edges, and validation of the solution.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>types.ts: Screen type definition</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The `Screen` type is a union of all possible screen states. The new \'blatov-task\' string literal was added to this union, allowing the application to manage the state for the Bl\303\241tov task screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
