  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 6
    user_intent: "Adding Minimum Spanning Tree Task\nThe user wants to add a new interactive task to the application focused on finding the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) of a graph. This involves:\n1.  Defining 5 levels of difficulty for the MST task, similar to the existing tasks and referencing the provided PDF for inspiration on graph structures and edge weighting.\n2.  Implementing the MST task component, which will include:\n    *   Graph visualization with weighted edges (e.g., representing cost or tiles).\n    *   User interaction to select edges to form a spanning tree.\n    *   Logic to check if the selected edges form a valid spanning tree and if its total weight is minimal.\n    *   Feedback mechanisms for correct/incorrect solutions and hints about MST algorithms (like Kruskal\'s or Prim\'s).\n3.  Integrating this new task into the application\'s navigation flow, making it accessible from the \"Models\" menu."
    session_summary: "### Summary of Coding Session: Map Constructor Error Fix and New Feature Implementation\n\nThis session focused on resolving a `TypeError: Constructor Map requires \'new\'` and subsequently adding a new feature for a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) task.\n\n**Key Accomplishments:**\n\n1.  **Resolved `Map` Constructor Error:**\n    *   The primary bug, `TypeError: Constructor Map requires \'new\'`, was identified and fixed.\n    *   The root cause was traced to an incorrect usage of the `Map` component (likely an icon from `lucide-react`) in `ModelsMenu.tsx` without proper import.\n    *   **Fixes implemented:**\n        *   Added `Map` to the `lucide-react` import in `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`.\n        *   Removed the unused `Map` import from `components/PathFindingTask.tsx` to prevent potential naming conflicts.\n\n2.  **Implemented New \"Minimum Spanning Tree\" (MST) Task:**\n    *   A new task, \"Minimum Spanning Tree,\" was added to the application, inspired by the provided PDF examples.\n    *   This involved creating a new component, `MSTTask.tsx`, and integrating it into the application\'s navigation flow.\n    *   **Features of the MST Task:**\n        *   **5 Levels of Difficulty:** Ranging from simple to complex graph structures.\n        *   **Weighted Edges:** Paths (edges) are assigned weights (e.g., \"number of tiles\" or \"cost\") to represent the cost of connection.\n        *   **Interactive Graph Visualization:** Users can select edges to build a spanning tree.\n        *   **Real-time Weight Calculation:** The current total weight of selected edges is displayed.\n        *   **Solution Validation:** The application checks if the selected edges form a valid spanning tree (connect all nodes without cycles) and if it\'s the *minimum* spanning tree based on Kruskal\'s algorithm logic.\n        *   **Feedback Mechanism:** Provides clear feedback on correctness, incorrectness, or if a lower-cost solution exists.\n        *   **Algorithm Explanation:** Includes a brief explanation of Kruskal\'s and Prim\'s algorithms.\n\n**Features Modified, Added, or Removed:**\n\n*   **Added:**\n    *   `MSTTask.tsx` component.\n    *   `\'mst-task\'` to the `Screen` type in `types.ts`.\n    *   Navigation logic for `\'mst-task\'` in `App.tsx`.\n    *   A new button and navigation handler (`onStartMST`) for the MST task in `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`.\n    *   New levels and corresponding data within `MSTTask.tsx`.\n*   **Modified:**\n    *   `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`: Updated props to include `onStartMST` and added the MST button to the UI.\n    *   `App.tsx`: Updated `renderScreen` switch statement to handle the `\'mst-task\'` screen.\n    *   `types.ts`: Added `\'mst-task\'` to the `Screen` type.\n    *   `components/PathFindingTask.tsx`: Removed unused `Map` import.\n    *   `components/BlatovTask.tsx`: Added a new irregular level (\"Ztracen\303\241 Lhota\") to the existing Blatov task.\n    *   `components/PathFindingTask.tsx`: Added a new irregular level (\"K\305\231ivolak\303\251 \303\272dol\303\255\") to the existing Path Finding task.\n\n**Dependencies and APIs:**\n\n*   `react`, `react-dom`\n*   `lucide-react` (for icons)\n*   `Tailwind CSS` (for styling)\n*   Standard JavaScript `Map` object (corrected usage)\n\n**Design Decisions:**\n\n*   Maintained a consistent component-based architecture.\n*   Utilized `useState` and `useMemo` for state management and performance optimization.\n*   Employed conditional rendering for screen transitions and dynamic feedback.\n*   Ensured a user-friendly interface with clear navigation and interactive elements.\n*   Integrated new features seamlessly into the existing navigation structure.\n\n**Environmental Variables:**\n\n*   None explicitly mentioned or required for these changes.\n\n**Security Preferences:**\n\n*   No security-sensitive operations were performed in this session.\n\n**Special User Requests and Preferences:**\n\n*   The user specifically requested the addition of a new task for finding the minimum spanning tree, with 5 levels of difficulty and weighted edges, similar to the provided PDF examples.\n*   The user also requested the addition of new irregular levels to the existing \"Path Finding\" and \"Blatov\" tasks, mirroring the complexity seen in the PDF.\n\n**Existing Blockers and Bugs:**\n\n*   The primary blocker (the `Map` constructor error) has been resolved.\n*   No new blockers were introduced.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n\n*   **Thoroughly test the new MST task:** Ensure all 5 levels function correctly, the MST logic (Kruskal\'s algorithm implementation) is sound, and the UI provides accurate feedback.\n*   **Review and Refactor:** If necessary, refactor the code for the new MST task and the updated Blatov/Path Finding levels for better readability and maintainability.\n*   **Cross-browser/Device Testing:** Verify the responsiveness and functionality across different browsers and devices.\n*   **Add more levels:** Consider adding more levels of difficulty for all graph-related tasks if required.\n*   **Improve visual feedback:** Enhance animations and visual cues for user interactions."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n<target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n<lines_modified>25-25</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Added \'mst-task\' to the Screen type definition.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n<target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>24-24;89-91;97-99</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Imported MSTTask component, added \'mst-task\' to the renderScreen switch statement, and updated ModelsMenu props to include onStartMST.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n<target_file>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>7-7;12-12;86-87</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Added onStartMST prop to ModelsMenuProps and included a button for the MST task in the menu.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n<target_file>/components/MSTTask.tsx</target_file>\n<lines_modified>1-426</lines_modified>\n<edit_summary>Created a new component MSTTask.tsx to implement the Minimum Spanning Tree task with 5 levels of difficulty, including Kruskal\'s algorithm for calculating the MST weight.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/types.ts</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-26</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This file defines the types used throughout the application, including the `Screen` type which was modified to include the new \'mst-task\' screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-196</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This is the main application component that handles screen navigation. It was updated to import and render the new MSTTask component and to add navigation logic for it.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-94</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This component displays the menu for different tasks. It was updated to include a new button for the MST task and to accept the corresponding `onStartMST` prop for navigation.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/components/BlatovTask.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-431</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This file contains the Blatov task (Spanning Tree). It was reviewed to understand the structure of graph-related tasks and to ensure consistency when creating the new MST task.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/components/PathFindingTask.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-428</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This file implements the pathfinding task. It was reviewed for structural similarities and patterns that could be applied to the new MST task.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n<absolute_path>/components/MSTTask.tsx</absolute_path>\n<lines_viewed>1-426</lines_viewed>\n<learnings>This is the newly created component for the Minimum Spanning Tree task. It implements 5 levels of difficulty, uses Kruskal\'s algorithm to calculate the MST weight, and provides user interaction for selecting edges.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>"
