  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Hover Interactions**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a bug within the `ParallelProcesses` component: hovering over transitions (the SVG rectangles) causes them to shift, hindering clicks. I\'m focusing on the component\'s code, particularly the interaction logic. The issue seems rooted in the mouse hover event handling and how it\'s affecting element positioning. My next step involves inspecting the transition element\'s event listeners and CSS.\n\n\n**Refining Hover Feedback**\n\nI\'ve isolated the cause of the element shifting during hover: the `hover:scale-110` class applied to the SVG group is misbehaving. I plan to remove this CSS-based scaling. Instead, I\'ll explore more stable methods, such as `transform-origin` adjustments or, ideally, using `motion.g` from `framer-motion` for smoother animation control. Alternatively, I may simply alter the stroke/color for hover feedback.\n\n\n**Implementing Hover Control**\n\nI\'ve decided to replace the CSS-based hover scaling with `framer-motion`\'s `motion.g` element and `whileHover={{ scale: 1.1 }}`. I\'m focusing on the `ParallelProcesses.tsx` file for the implementation. My plan involves replacing the current `g` element and the CSS class and its interaction logic. I\'m also addressing the user\'s feedback by adding an invisible, larger hit area to the transitions to improve clickability. I\'m confident that this resolves the main issue.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
