  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 7
    user_intent: "Parallel Processes Simulation\nThe user wants to create an interactive simulation of a factory\'s filling and capping process using Petri nets. This involves:\n1.  Adding a new \"Parallel Processes\" task to the application\'s \"Models\" menu.\n2.  Implementing the simulation with a visual Petri net diagram.\n3.  Ensuring the simulation accurately reflects the described factory workflow, including the movement of \"crates\" (tokens) through filling, intermediate storage, and capping stages.\n4.  Making the simulation interactive, allowing users to trigger actions (transitions) by clicking on them.\n5.  Enhancing the visualization with icons, larger diagram size, and animations to clearly show the process flow, durations of actions, and progress.\n6.  Implementing a mechanism to return a token to the start after a crate is moved to the warehouse.\n7.  Fixing bugs related to the interactivity and visual presentation of the simulation elements."
    session_summary: "## Summary of Coding Session: Enhancing the Parallel Processes Simulation\n\nThis session focused on refining the \"Parallel Processes\" simulation, primarily involving the implementation and enhancement of a Petri net model for a bottle-filling and capping factory.\n\n**Key Accomplishments:**\n\n1.  **New Task Integration:**\n    *   The `\'parallel-processes\'` screen type was added to `types.ts`.\n    *   Navigation for this new screen was integrated into `App.tsx`.\n    *   A corresponding button and navigation handler (`onStartParallel`) were added to `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`.\n\n2.  **Parallel Processes Component Development (`components/ParallelProcesses.tsx`):**\n    *   **Initial Implementation:** A functional Petri net simulation was created based on the user\'s description of a bottle-filling and capping factory. This included defining places (states) and transitions (actions) with initial token distribution.\n    *   **Bug Fixes:**\n        *   Resolved an issue where transitions were visually shifting on hover, making them difficult to click. This was achieved by using `motion.g` with proper `transformOrigin` and adding an invisible larger click target.\n        *   Ensured the \"Vstup\" (input) token is returned after the \"Napln\304\233n\303\241 bedna\" is moved, by modifying the `t2` transition\'s outputs in the Petri net definition.\n    *   **Feature Enhancements:**\n        *   **Thematic Icons:** Added relevant icons (Package, Warehouse, Settings, Truck, Droplets, Lock) to places and transitions to visually represent factory elements and actions.\n        *   **Diagram Enlargement & Readability:** Increased the overall size of the SVG canvas and elements (places, icons, text) for better clarity.\n        *   **Action Durations & Animations:**\n            *   Introduced `duration` property for each transition, defining the time an action takes.\n            *   Implemented a visual progress bar animation within the transition rectangles to show the time elapsed during an action.\n            *   Added a \"PROB\303\215H\303\201...\" (IN PROGRESS...) text indicator during active transitions.\n            *   Refined hover and tap animations for transitions.\n        *   **State Management:** Replaced `isAnimating` with `activeTransitionId` for more precise control over which transition is currently active and being animated.\n\n**Features Modified, Added, or Removed:**\n\n*   **Added:**\n    *   `\'parallel-processes\'` to `Screen` type in `types.ts`.\n    *   `ParallelProcesses` component.\n    *   Navigation logic for `\'parallel-processes\'` in `App.tsx`.\n    *   `onStartParallel` prop and button in `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`.\n    *   `duration` property to `Transition` interface.\n    *   `activeTransitionId` state in `ParallelProcesses.tsx`.\n    *   Thematic icons for places and transitions.\n    *   Progress bar animation and \"PROB\303\215H\303\201...\" text for active transitions.\n    *   Enlarged SVG canvas and elements.\n*   **Modified:**\n    *   `components/ParallelProcesses.tsx`: Extensive modifications for functionality, visuals, and animations.\n    *   `components/ModelsMenu.tsx`: Added a new button for the \"Paraleln\303\255 procesy\" task.\n    *   `App.tsx`: Integrated the new screen and its navigation.\n    *   `types.ts`: Added the new screen type.\n*   **Removed:**\n    *   `isAnimating` state, replaced by `activeTransitionId`.\n\n**Dependencies and APIs:**\n\n*   `react`, `react-dom`\n*   `lucide-react` (for icons)\n*   `motion` (from `motion/react` for animations)\n*   `Tailwind CSS` (for styling)\n*   Standard JavaScript `Map` object.\n\n**Design Decisions:**\n\n*   **Petri Nets:** Utilized Petri nets as the core modeling paradigm for simulating concurrent processes.\n*   **SVG for Visualization:** Employed SVG for rendering the Petri net diagram, allowing for precise control over element placement and animation.\n*   **`framer-motion` (now `motion/react`):** Leveraged for smooth animations and transitions, enhancing user experience.\n*   **Component-Based Architecture:** Maintained a clear separation of concerns with dedicated components for different parts of the application.\n*   **State Management:** Used `useState` for managing the simulation\'s state (places, tokens, history, active transition).\n\n**Environmental Variables:**\n\n*   None explicitly used or required for these changes.\n\n**Security Preferences:**\n\n*   No security-sensitive operations were performed.\n\n**Special User Requests and Preferences:**\n\n*   Add a \"Paraleln\303\255 procesy\" task with a factory simulation based on a provided description.\n*   The simulation should use Petri nets.\n*   The user should be able to interact by moving tokens.\n*   Fix bugs related to transition interaction (hover/click issues).\n*   Return the input token after a specific action (\"Uskladn\304\233n\303\255\").\n*   Add thematic icons to represent factory elements.\n*   Enlarge the diagram for better readability.\n*   Add animations and time durations for actions to visualize the process flow.\n\n**Existing Blockers and Bugs:**\n\n*   All previously identified bugs have been addressed. The simulation is now functional and visually enhanced.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n\n*   **Testing:** Thoroughly test the simulation across different browsers and devices to ensure consistent performance and visual fidelity.\n*   **Refinement:** Potentially add more complex scenarios or error handling within the Petri net logic if required.\n*   **User Feedback:** Gather feedback on the current implementation and make further adjustments based on user experience.\n*   **Code Cleanup:** Review the code for any potential optimizations or refactoring opportunities."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/types.ts</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>25-25</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Added \'parallel-processes\' to the Screen type definition.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/App.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>24-24;89-91;97-99</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Imported ParallelProcesses component, added \'parallel-processes\' to the renderScreen switch statement, and updated ModelsMenu props to include onStartParallel.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>7-7;12-12;86-87</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Added onStartParallel prop to ModelsMenuProps and included a button for the Parallel Processes task in the menu.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/components/ParallelProcesses.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>1-325</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Created ParallelProcesses.tsx component to simulate a factory process using Petri nets, including interactive elements, icons, and animations.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/components/ParallelProcesses.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>193-225</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Fixed transition hover and click target issues by using motion.g and adding a larger invisible click area.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/components/ParallelProcesses.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>32-37</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Updated the \'Uskladn\304\233n\303\255\' transition to return a token to \'Vstup\' after the process is complete.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n    <target_file>/components/ParallelProcesses.tsx</target_file>\n    <lines_modified>1-325</lines_modified>\n    <edit_summary>Enlarged the diagram for better readability, added transition durations, and implemented progress animations for active transitions.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n    <absolute_path>/types.ts</absolute_path>\n    <lines_viewed>1-26</lines_viewed>\n    <learnings>This file defines the application\'s types, including the `Screen` type. It was updated to include the new \'parallel-processes\' screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n    <absolute_path>/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n    <lines_viewed>1-196</lines_viewed>\n    <learnings>This is the main application component responsible for screen navigation. It was updated to import and render the `ParallelProcesses` component and to add the necessary navigation logic.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n    <absolute_path>/components/ModelsMenu.tsx</absolute_path>\n    <lines_viewed>1-94</lines_viewed>\n    <learnings>This component displays the menu for different tasks. It was updated to include a new button for the \'Parallel Processes\' task and to accept the corresponding `onStartParallel` prop for navigation.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_file>\n    <absolute_path>/components/ParallelProcesses.tsx</absolute_path>\n    <lines_viewed>1-325</lines_viewed>\n    <learnings>This is the core component for the \'Parallel Processes\' task, implementing a Petri net simulation of a factory line. It was iteratively updated to fix bugs, add icons, enlarge the diagram, and implement animations and time durations for actions.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>Screen type in /types.ts</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The `Screen` type needed to be updated to include the new \'parallel-processes\' screen identifier to enable navigation to this new task.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>App.tsx navigation logic</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The `App.tsx` file required updates to import the `ParallelProcesses` component and to add a `case` statement in the `renderScreen` function to handle navigation to the \'parallel-processes\' screen.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>ModelsMenu.tsx button and prop</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The `ModelsMenu` component needed a new button for \'Parallel Processes\' and its corresponding `onStartParallel` prop to trigger navigation.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>ParallelProcesses.tsx component structure</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>This component implements the Petri net simulation. Key parts include the `Place` and `Transition` interfaces, `INITIAL_PLACES` and `TRANSITIONS` data, `isEnabled` function to check transition readiness, `fireTransition` function to execute transitions, and the SVG rendering logic.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>ParallelProcesses.tsx transition animation and click handling</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The initial implementation of transition scaling on hover was causing the elements to shift. This was fixed by using `motion.g` with `transformOrigin` and adding an invisible larger click target (`rect`) to ensure reliable interaction.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>ParallelProcesses.tsx token return logic</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The \'Uskladn\304\233n\303\255\' transition (t2) was modified to include \'s0\' in its `outputs` array, ensuring a token is returned to the \'Vstup\' place after the bed is moved to the warehouse, allowing the process to loop.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n    <node_identifier>ParallelProcesses.tsx diagram scaling and animation</node_identifier>\n    <learnings>The SVG `viewBox` was increased, and coordinates for places and transitions were adjusted to enlarge the diagram. Transition durations were added to the `Transition` interface, and a progress bar animation (`motion.rect`) was implemented within the transition rendering to visualize the time spent on each action.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
